  "text": "Veterinary Oncology in Matthews, North Carolina | Pet Oncologist\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nAbout\nOur Hospital\nVeterinary Specialists\nEmergency Veterinarians\nWhat Sets Us Apart\nMurray's Fund\nHospital Tour\nSpecialties\nNeurology\nSurgery\nOncology\nRadiation Therapy\nCardiology\nInternal Medicine\nEmergencies\nDiagnostics\nReferrals\nPatients\nPatient Information\nPay Online\nFinancing Options\nBlog\nCareers\nContact\nSearch\nSearch\nFacebook\nInstagram\n×\nClose\nSearch\nSearch\nSkip to Main Content\nAccessible Version\nStandard Version\n4099 Campus Ridge Rd\nMatthews\nNC\n28104\nUS\n(704) 815-3939\nFacebook\nInstagram\nOpen Search Dialog\nShop\nLocations\nCharlotte\nGreensboro\nHuntersville\nMatthews\nRock Hill\nWinston-Salem\nAbout\nOur Hospital\nVeterinary Specialists\nEmergency Veterinarians\nWhat Sets Us Apart\nMurray's Fund\nHospital Tour\nSpecialties\nNeurology\nSurgery\nOncology\nRadiation Therapy\nCardiology\nInternal Medicine\nEmergencies\nDiagnostics\nReferrals\nPatients\nPatient Information\nPay Online\nFinancing Options\nBlog\nCareers\nContact\nOpen 7 Days a Week - Including Saturday & Sunday\nVeterinary Oncology\nAdvanced Cancer Care for North Carolina Pets\nThe oncology department at\nCarolina Veterinary Specialists\nin Matthews uses cutting-edge diagnostics and treatments to provide pets with cancer the best possible care.\nPLEASE NOTE: A\nreferral\nfrom your primary care veterinarian is required before making an oncology appointment.\nBook an Appointment\nOur Oncology Services\nCancer. It’s a disease that affects humans and animals, and it can affect even the healthiest ones. The good news is that it can be treated with a number of advanced methods.\nOur veterinary oncologists are committed to providing care and treatment of pets with cancer, and support for the individuals and families that love them. They work closely with our board-certified radiation oncologist and other specialists to ensure your pet receives the best possible care.\nAfter reviewing your pet’s medical history and diagnosis we will sit down with you and your pet to discuss the disease, staging (additional diagnostics), treatment options, side effects and prognosis.\nOur Board-Certified Veterinary Oncologists\nA board-certified veterinary oncologist has completed extensive training after veterinary school that focuses on oncology (how cancer develops and how to treat it). Throughout this training, an oncologist is also required to complete an internship and specialized residency, pass comprehensive exams, and complete publication requirements to become board-certified in Medical Oncology by the American College of Veterinary Internal Medicine (ACVIM).\nMeet Dr. Claudia McFadden\nMeet Dr. Shannon Parfitt\nMeet Dr. Timothy Estabrooks\nStaging (Additional Diagnostics)\nAfter a diagnosis of cancer, additional\ndiagnostic testing\ncan help to determine the extent of cancer in the body, which allows us to optimize treatment recommendations and better predict prognosis.\nTreatment Options\nWhen staging is complete our team of specialists will discuss all the appropriate treatment options. Cancer can be treated by several different therapies or combination of treatments including\nsurgery\n, chemotherapy,\nradiation therapy\n, immunotherapy, targeted therapies or palliative care when appropriate.\nWhat is vetIQure™ Tumour Specific Electroporation (TSE)?\nCarolina Veterinary Specialists offers vetIQure™ Tumour Specific Electroporation (TSE), an advanced, targeted therapy designed to enhance the delivery of therapeutic agents directly into cancer cells while minimizing effects on surrounding healthy tissue. Using precisely controlled electrical pulses, TSE temporarily increases tumor cell permeability, allowing medications to enter more effectively and support a localized treatment approach. This technology promotes a controlled cellular response (apoptosis) rather than indiscriminate tissue destruction.\nWhy choose vetIQure™ Tumour Specific Electroporation (TSE)?\nTSE may be considered for tumors in sensitive or surgically challenging locations, when clear surgical margins are difficult to achieve, or as part of a comprehensive cancer care plan.\nOur board-certified oncology team carefully evaluates each patient to determine whether TSE is appropriate, ensuring a personalized and compassionate approach to your pet’s cancer treatment.\nFinancial Support For Veterinary Oncology Treatments\nDr. Claudia McFadden developed Murray's Fund to help clients financially afford their pet's oncology treatments. If your pet has been diagnosed with cancer, check out how Murray's Fund can help.\nLearn More\n« Go Back\nSpecialties\nNeurology\nSurgery\nOncology\nRadiation Therapy\nCardiology\nInternal Medicine\nHappy Tails from Clients\n\"Took great care of our fur baby on the biggest holiday of the year. And even though we’re now dealing with the diagnosis and management of diabetes, they were great to make sure we knew how to care for her now. Kudos!\"\n- Nelson B.\nCaring for Pets in Matthews\nCarolina Veterinary Specialists\nin Matthews accepts new clients to our specialty services by referral only. Our emergency service accepts all clients.\nContact Us\nHome\nAbout\nSpecialties\nEmergencies\nDiagnostics\nReferrals\nCareers\nContact\nCarolina Veterinary Specialists\n4099 Campus Ridge Rd\nMatthews\nNC\n28104\nUS\nTerms and Conditions\nDo Not Sell or Share My Personal Information\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility\nSearch\nSitemap\nBack to Top\nFacebook\nInstagram\nCopyright © 2026. All Rights Reserved.\nPart of the\nPetVet Care Centers Network\n.\n(704) 815-3939\nContact\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu",
